---
/**
 * Terms of Sale for the marketing landing.
 *
 * These terms cover the one-time purchase of the LaunchKit source code
 * through this site. They are deliberately NOT the SaaS terms of service
 * that ship inside launchkit-web (`/terms` in the app) — there are no
 * accounts, uploads or subscriptions here, only a purchase, a delivery and
 * a license.
 *
 * Update `lastUpdated` whenever you change the copy. Replace `jurisdiction`
 * with your real legal seat before launch, and have counsel read the
 * executed LICENSE this page defers to.
 */
import Legal from "@/layouts/legal.astro"
import { site } from "@/config/site"

const lastUpdated = "2026-09-03"
const contactEmail = site.social.email
const jurisdiction = "the jurisdiction where the seller is registered"
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of Sale"
  description="The terms that govern buying LaunchKit through this site."
  eyebrow={`Last updated · ${lastUpdated}`}
>
  <p>
    These terms apply to every purchase of {site.brand} made through
    {site.domain}. By completing checkout you agree to them, and to the
    commercial license that governs the code itself (summarised at{" "}
    <a href="/license">/license</a>; the executed text ships as
    <code>LICENSE</code> in each repository).
  </p>

  <h2>1. What you are buying</h2>
  <p>
    A one-time, non-transferable commercial license to the {site.brand} source code
    — two repositories, <code>launchkit-api</code> and
    <code>launchkit-web</code> — delivered as read access to a private GitHub organization.
    This is not a subscription: there are no recurring charges and nothing to cancel.
    The tier you choose (Solo or Unlimited) sets how many products you may build with
    it and which support channels are included; the code itself, the repository access
    and the update stream are the same on both.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Payment</h2>
  <p>
    Payment is processed by Stripe, our payment processor. We never see or store
    your card details. Prices are shown in US dollars and, where required by
    law, Stripe adds and collects applicable VAT, GST or sales tax at checkout.
    You will receive a receipt and, if enabled, an invoice by email.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Delivery and access</h2>
  <p>
    Within minutes of a successful payment you receive an email with a claim
    link. Enter your GitHub username there and we invite that account to the
    private organization. Access is personal to you: keep your GitHub account
    secure, and don't share organization access with third parties. If you need
    to move your license to a different GitHub account, email us.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Because the product is source code, we cannot take it back once it has been
    delivered. Refunds are therefore available only <em>before</em> you claim access:
    if you change your mind, email us within 7 days of checkout and we refund in full.
    Once you have been invited to the private organization, all sales are final. Read
    the FAQ and email us with questions before buying — we answer every message.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Updates and support</h2>
  <p>
    Both tiers receive new releases for as long as {site.brand} is maintained, with
    no renewal and no expiry, plus email support. Unlimited adds the private Discord,
    early access to new features and a vote on the roadmap. Security fixes go to every
    license holder regardless of tier. We don't promise a specific release cadence
    or that any particular feature will be built.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    {site.brand} and its source code remain our property; you receive a license, not
    ownership. Everything you build on top of it is yours — you may sell, host and
    modify your applications without restriction and without crediting us. The codebase
    includes third-party open source components under their own licenses (MIT, BSD
    and similar); those terms apply to those components.
  </p>

  <h2>7. What you may not do</h2>
  <p>
    You may not resell, sublicense or redistribute the boilerplate itself — as a
    starter kit, template, code generator or competing product — or publish the
    source code as-is. You may not share your organization access, and you may
    not remove proprietary notices from any redistribution. The full list of
    permissions and restrictions is in the license.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Termination</h2>
  <p>
    If you breach the license — for example by redistributing the code or
    sharing access — we may remove you from the private organization and
    terminate your right to receive updates and support. The license terms
    continue to govern any copies of the code you already hold.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    The software is provided <em>as is</em>, without warranty of any kind,
    express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular
    purpose and non-infringement. We do not warrant that it is error-free, that
    it meets any regulatory requirement, or that it will be maintained for any
    particular period.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect,
    incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits,
    data or business, arising from your purchase or use of the software. Our
    total liability under these terms and the license is limited to the amount
    you paid for it.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms for future purchases. Changes that affect existing
    license holders — for example to the support terms — will be communicated by
    email at least 14 days before they take effect.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of {jurisdiction}. Any dispute arising
    from a purchase will be resolved in the courts of {jurisdiction}.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms? Reach us at{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
